{"id": "EUVD-2026-108836", "enisaUuid": "7c94f1f4-3d5c-3387-999f-d5ebc5505068", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nip6_gre: remove obsolete ERSPAN PMTU update\n\nA tc tunnel_key action can attach a METADATA_IP_TUNNEL dst to an skb,\nand mirred can redirect it to a native ip6erspan device. The legacy PMTU\nupdate in ip6erspan_tunnel_xmit() treats that metadata dst as a route.\nSince it has no output device, dst_dev(dst)->mtu dereferences NULL.\n\nOn v7.2 with KASAN, an initial UID/GID 65534 process with CapEff 0 used\nself-created user and network namespaces to trigger:\n\n  KASAN: null-ptr-deref\n  RIP: ip6erspan_tunnel_xmit+0x10fc/0x2cc0\n  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt\n\nThe update is obsolete. Commit fe1a4ca0a2b7 (\"ip6_gre: process toobig\nin a better way\") changed IPv6 GRE Too Big handling to update the\nunderlay route and removed the equivalent block from __gre6_xmit().\nip6_tnl_xmit() then propagates the underlay PMTU to the overlay route.\n\nRemove the stale ERSPAN copy and its now-unused dst variable. This\neliminates the metadata-dst dereference and keeps ERSPAN aligned with\nIPv6 GRE PMTU handling.", "datePublished": "2026-10-23T12:22:00", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-23T12:22:00", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b14a682ad7d45345701e08f9279d483a1da8b36c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f5b143f4cd3fb7673df8d727550478a4b762908a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2d06cb25a497d3a7034ef9d172626c2d6620a0f1", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8f27260b989f488760289276377db24fbfb20bfa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8bc60db48e8cba35488bbd6e1f94aa990afa275a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-99041"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.0, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "01ce08f8-cc9e-3016-a632-4e8f946d9217", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a963eb61b7c39e6c422b6e48619d19d04719358 <b14a682ad7d45345701e08f9279d483a1da8b36c"}, {"id": "0674f2d4-4452-3578-b975-05f59a980484", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a963eb61b7c39e6c422b6e48619d19d04719358 <8bc60db48e8cba35488bbd6e1f94aa990afa275a"}, {"id": "401b3c1b-f560-32ba-a16d-fe2889ce36a1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "8565183e-b58d-3499-8069-19e4b6238427", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "866b3819-41ca-320e-a16e-c742de0c857b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a963eb61b7c39e6c422b6e48619d19d04719358 <f5b143f4cd3fb7673df8d727550478a4b762908a"}, {"id": "89f3728c-6b30-33dc-8102-99086b300e94", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.11"}, {"id": "9102e976-1088-3bba-8b27-57036efab7ab", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a963eb61b7c39e6c422b6e48619d19d04719358 <8f27260b989f488760289276377db24fbfb20bfa"}, {"id": "928d61d9-dd35-3881-98a6-966bf0a37348", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "a3c8716a-55ba-3df4-a43b-1d86799febc6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "ac77133b-8d2f-3bfc-806a-7bc294fc0d65", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5a963eb61b7c39e6c422b6e48619d19d04719358 <2d06cb25a497d3a7034ef9d172626c2d6620a0f1"}, {"id": "d66217ee-5949-3cb1-9c90-04bcdf7320c4", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.58"}, {"id": "fd1ec04a-9acd-393b-b331-5612af0b18fd", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "4.16"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "341e6bca-8fb8-35f2-a101-06b176ad853e", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}